WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.530
By UN figures, there were 304 million
international migrants in 2024.

2
00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:10.750
That is up from 275 million in 2020.

3
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.630
It sounds enormous.

4
00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:16.770
Yet it is only 3.7 per cent
of the world's population:

5
00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:19.370
about one person in 27.

6
00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:23.790
So why do some people move,
while most stay where they are?

7
00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:25.810
Is it mainly to escape war?

8
00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:27.360
Is it climate change?

9
00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:31.610
In this mission, you'll sort
migrants into voluntary and forced,

10
00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:35.910
and tell economic migrants from
refugees and asylum seekers.

11
00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:40.950
Then you'll use a country's migration
figures to explain who leaves, and why.

12
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:46.290
Your mission: explain why some people
move to another country while most stay.
